Warning [jet.PositionalBoolParameter]: Public function `early` has a positional `Bool` parameter `ready`
  --> tests/ui_lint/unused_parameter_match_subject.jet:24:11
    |
 24 | early: fn(ready: Bool, value: Int, unused: Int) -> Int {
    |           ^^^^^
 Why: Positional booleans are easy to transpose at the call site
 Fix: Callers can write `ready: true` to make the intent clear (S61 labels)
More: jet-lang.dev/e/L2401

Warning [jet.UnusedParameter]: Parameter `unused` is never used.
  --> tests/ui_lint/unused_parameter_match_subject.jet:24:36
    |
 24 | early: fn(ready: Bool, value: Int, unused: Int) -> Int {
    |                                    ^^^^^^
 Why: An unused parameter often means the function contract or implementation is incomplete; Jet keeps this warning-only so prototypes stay unblocked.
 Fix: Use `unused`, rename it to `_unused` when it is intentionally unused, or remove it from the function contract.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/L0102

